one enormous ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d57\"},\"ref\":\"d57\",\"snippet\":\" ... Books by non-white authors have over seven times the likelihood of shortlisting compared to other books (OR: 7.68; p < 0.05). In turn, a book by a non-white author has over 10 times the likelihood of winning the Booker prize compared to other books (OR ... \",\"title\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10837049/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d85\"},\"ref\":\"d85\",\"snippet\":\" ... Man Booker Prize, winner, The Sense of an Ending\\n*2011 Costa Book Awards, shortlist, The Sense of an Ending\\n*2012: Europese Literatuurprijs\\n*2015: Zinklar Award at the first annual Blixen Ceremony in Copenhagen\\n*2016: Siegfried Lenz Prize\\n*2017: Officier in the Ordre National de la Légion d'Honneur ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julian_Barnes\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"5ca0d7653c581c9a29c76cf7f90d9992e284cf514b6c03b2fb2fba24336f8cf9\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"0e0cb97a342c6416a6b88937de67cfffd31eae6518a0447fad25251e62e0e493\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Man Booker International 2016 shortlist Yan Lianke The Four Books\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d86\"},\"ref\":\"d86\",\"snippet\":\" ... Conditional' in her 2001 Booker shortlisted novel Hotel World – lines which could only be written by one who knows:\\n\\nAbout you – continued…\\n\\nIf you need help filling out this form, or any part of it, phone…\\n\\nTell us about yourself.\\n\\nWell. I am a nice person.\\n\\nThe protagonist ... \",\"title\":\"https://emmaashmere.com/category/on-writing/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d30\"},\"ref\":\"d30\",\"snippet\":\" ... Shortlist | Jhumpa Lahiri | The Lowland | Bloomsbury | *Robert Macfarlane (chair) *Martha Kearney *Stuart Kelly *Natalie Haynes *Robert Douglas-Fairhurst |\\n| 2013 The Booker Prizes |url= |url-status=live |archive-url= |archive-date=4 April 2023 |access-date=2022-10-19 |website=thebookerprizes.com |language=en}} | Shortlist | Ruth Ozeki | A Tale ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d87\"},\"ref\":\"d87\",\"snippet\":\" ... Award for Best Novella 2016. My first novel, Sealed (2017), is a work of eco-horror, which was shortlisted for the Not the Booker Award 2018. My second novel, Exit Management (2020), moves between contemporary Britain and 1940s Budapest. It was named a Fiction Book of the Year ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.durham.ac.uk/staff/naomi-r-booth/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d57\"},\"ref\":\"d57\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2021; Lauter 1991; Nishikawa 2021; Sapiro 2016). Although in our data non-white authors disproportionately shortlist for and win the Booker prize (and over the period also make up a bigger share of the nominations), in a supplementary analysis we find that publishers who were regularly submitting to ... \",\"title\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10837049/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d37\"},\"ref\":\"d37\",\"snippet\":\" ... s exuberant, coruscating translation.\\n\\n\\\"This is a luminous novel of India and Partition, but one whose spellbinding brio and fierce compassion weaves youth and age, male and female, family and nation into a kaleidoscopic whole.\\\"\\n\\nThe International Booker Prize 2022 Shortlist\\n\\n| Title | Author | Translator | Original Language | Author Residence ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d5\"},\"ref\":\"d5\",\"snippet\":\" ... Literary critics have noted that it is a mark of distinction for authors to be selected for inclusion in the shortlist or to be nominated for the \\\"longlist\\\".\\n\\nA sister prize, the International Booker Prize, is awarded for a work of fiction translated into English and published in ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d6\"},\"ref\":\"d6\",\"snippet\":\" ... Having been a symbol of desolation, it's become a symbol of hope.\\\"\\\"Sudbury a symbol of hope: Margaret Atwood\\\" . Northern Life, November 23, 2009. Atwood has been chair of the Writers' Union of Canada and helped to found the Canadian English-speaking chapter of PEN International, a ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Atwood\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d62\"},\"r